| !Run for !VCMI - RISC OS port of VCMI, the open-source Heroes of Might
| and Magic III engine. Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf),
| statically linked with riscos-mesa's SDL2 and converted to an Absolute
| (AIF) file, so !SharedLibs isn't needed.

Set VCMI$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <VCMI$Dir>.!Sprites

| --- Game data --------------------------------------------------------
| VCMI needs the files of Heroes of Might and Magic III: Shadow of Death
| or Complete (GOG, CD). Copy the Data, Maps and Mp3 directories into
| H3data inside this application (see H3data.ReadMe), or put them anywhere
| and *Set VCMI$Data to the directory that holds them (e.g. in your !Boot).
If "<VCMI$Data>"="" Then Set VCMI$Data <VCMI$Dir>.H3data
| Settings, saved games and logs go in <Choices$Write>.VCMI.

| --- Threads ----------------------------------------------------------
| The computer players think on threads (UnixLib), and SDL plays sound on
| one. PThreadTicker keeps them running while the game waits for the
| desktop. Loaded from !System if there, else ours.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <VCMI$Dir>.PThrTicker

| --- Sound ------------------------------------------------------------
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer, StreamManager and SharedSound
| (in !System), mixed with other programs' sound. SharedSound is part of
| RISC OS; SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager are in ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html. Without them the
| game plays silently.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| --- Scaling with the overlay (Raspberry Pi) ---------------------------
| With "Scale with the overlay" on (System Options) and a Resolution
| smaller than the screen in full screen, riscos-mesa scales the picture
| through VideoOverlay. Loaded from !System if there.
RMEnsure VideoOverlay 0.00 IfThere System:Modules.VideoOverlay Then RMLoad System:Modules.VideoOverlay

| --- Logging ----------------------------------------------------------
| VCMI always writes its own log, <Choices$Write>.VCMI.Cache.VCMI_Client_log/txt.
| For the program's other output too (useful when reporting a problem),
| remove the | from the next line: it goes in <Wimp$ScrapDir>.vcmilog.
| Set VCMI$LogOn 1
Unset VCMI$Log
If "<VCMI$LogOn>"<>"" Then Set VCMI$Log /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>/vcmilog
Unset VCMI$LogOn

| --- Memory -----------------------------------------------------------
| The C heap goes in dynamic areas ("VCMI Heap", "VCMI Heap 2"...), so
| the WimpSlot only holds the program and its stack.
WimpSlot -min 48000K -max 48000K

| For the log: when !Run started (the log says when the game did).
Set VCMI$RunAt <Sys$Time>
Do Run <VCMI$Dir>.vcmi %*0
